# NOTE: Docker anchors ignore patterns to the build-context root, so a bare
# `node_modules` matches ONLY ./node_modules. pnpm keeps per-package stores at
# packages/*/node_modules, which then still get sent to the daemon and, via
# `COPY . .`, overwrite the correct in-image symlinks with host symlinks that
# point at Windows paths (e.g. /d/OpenMAIC/node_modules/.pnpm/...). Those are
# dangling inside Linux and break `pnpm run build:packages` with
# "Cannot find module '.../packages/<pkg>/node_modules/rollup/dist/bin/rollup'".
# Any pattern that must cover nested directories therefore needs a `**/` prefix.

# dependencies
**/node_modules
**/.pnpm-store

# build output
# `out` / `build` stay root-anchored on purpose: they are generic names that a
# future source directory could legitimately use, and no nested one exists today.
**/.next
out
**/dist
build
**/coverage
**/.turbo

# git
.git
.gitignore

# IDE / agent tooling
.idea
.vscode
**/.codegraph
**/.workbuddy

# env & secrets
.env*
!.env.example
server-providers*.yml

# misc
assets
*.md
*.pdf
*.pem
.DS_Store
.vercel
logs
data
docs
.claude

# isolated MP4 render service — built as its own image (render-service/Dockerfile),
# never part of the main app image.
render-service
